<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38571" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prodrŏmus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόδρομος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A certain north-northeast wind that blows eight days
				before the rising of the dog-star</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prodromi nulli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 6, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 47, 47, §
			123</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of early fig</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				26, 49, § 113</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
